sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as Your text
    participant Tok as Tokenizer
    participant Vocab as Vocabulary
    participant Emb as Embedding table
    participant M as Model
    U->>Tok: "unbelievable"
    Tok->>Vocab: greedy merge of byte pairs
    Vocab-->>Tok: ["un", "bel", "iev", "able"]
    Note over Tok,Vocab: common words are one token, rare ones fragment — that is why cost varies by language
    Tok->>Emb: token ids
    Emb-->>M: a vector per token
    M-->>Tok: predicted next token id
    Tok-->>U: detokenised text
    Note over U,M: the model never sees characters, only ids — hence the trouble counting letters
